# Engineering Authority

Every implementation session must begin by reading the Engineering Authority.

**Full index:** [docs/engineering/README.md](../../docs/engineering/README.md)

## Before Writing Code

Read in order:

1. [docs/engineering/CURRENT_MILESTONE.md](../../docs/engineering/CURRENT_MILESTONE.md)
2. [docs/engineering/ACTIVE_PR.md](../../docs/engineering/ACTIVE_PR.md)
3. [docs/engineering/ARCHITECTURE.md](../../docs/engineering/ARCHITECTURE.md)
4. [docs/engineering/STANDARDS.md](../../docs/engineering/STANDARDS.md)

**Canonical endpoint architecture (do not duplicate):** [docs/communications/ark-voice-endpoint-architecture-v1.md](../../docs/communications/ark-voice-endpoint-architecture-v1.md)

## After Implementation

Append an entry to [docs/engineering/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md](../../docs/engineering/IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md).

Every entry must include: date, PR, files changed, reason, architecture impact, outstanding questions.

## Do Not Modify (Unless Explicitly Instructed)

- ADRs in `docs/engineering/adr/` — **never edit accepted ADRs**; supersede with a new ADR
- [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../docs/engineering/ARCHITECTURE.md) — architecture review required
- [STANDARDS.md](../../docs/engineering/STANDARDS.md) — architecture review required

Architecture documents are reviewed. Implementation documents (`CURRENT_MILESTONE.md`, `ACTIVE_PR.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION_LOG.md`) are updated.

## Stop Discipline

- Never continue into another PR or milestone.
- Stop after completing the requested PR scope in [ACTIVE_PR.md](../../docs/engineering/ACTIVE_PR.md).
- One milestone · one PR · one review · stop.
